-- ============================================================================
-- Migration: Sheet Metal Lookup Tables -- material handling, process-material
--            feasibility, min hole diameter, part spacing (staging)
-- Purpose: Lands 5 tables from a newly-supplied combined export into the same
--          lossless staging table earlier migrations created. See migration
--          479's header for the staging/promotion architecture. No vendor
--          name present in this source file.
--
--          4 near-duplicate standalone files (tblMaterialHandling.json,
--          tblMaterialHandlingBySize.json, tblMaterialProcessAllowed.json,
--          tblMinHoleDiameterRatio.json) were also supplied separately and
--          contain the SAME data as 4 of these 5 tables -- not staged again,
--          this migration is the single source of truth for them.
--
--          Per-table consumer check:
--          - tblMaterialHandlingByWeight (6 rows, load time (s) by weight):
--            no material-handling-time cost concept exists in this app's
--            process costing today (see also migration 515's
--            handling_allowance $USD tables, and migration 520's Bend-Brake-
--            specific version -- three overlapping-but-not-identical
--            "handling by weight" exports now exist; see PLAN.md Phase 2a
--            for which one is actually promoted).
--          - tblMaterialHandlingBySize (10 rows, handling time (s) by
--            length x width x thickness): a DIFFERENT axis (part footprint,
--            not weight) -- no consumer either.
--          - tblMaterialProcessAllowed (7 rows, material code -> which
--            processes are allowed): OxyFuel/Plasma Cut have no cost engine
--            in this app at all regardless of this table; Laser/Waterjet/
--            Fiber Laser all already have real engines with no material
--            gate today. No consumer, reference only.
--          - tblMinHoleDiameterRatio (5 rows, material UTS (MPa) -> min
--            hole-diameter-to-thickness ratio): real punch-tooling physics
--            (grepped turret-punch-engine.ts, dfm-scoring.service.ts,
--            cad-analysis.service.ts -- no min-diameter-to-thickness concept
--            exists anywhere). This is the real data behind closeout Plan
--            Phase 1 (min-hole-diameter DFM check) -- staged here, promoted
--            separately once that phase is implemented.
--          - tblPartSpacing (~150 rows, process + thickness -> minimum part
--            spacing for nesting): this app's real nesting spacing
--            (computePartAllowanceMm in sheet-metal-nesting.engine.ts) uses
--            one continuous shear-strength-based formula for every process,
--            not this per-process table. This is the real data behind
--            closeout Plan Phase 3 (nesting part-spacing reconciliation) --
--            staged here, promoted separately.
